{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789306415,"nonce":"El5V9QqDowxe2njVBciizscev+0=","title":"A loop's generic copy is entered mid-way without the values its merge blocks read","message":"inline_known_calls versions a loop that holds inlinable sites; each site's guard failure runs the generic call in the fast world and jumps into the slow copy after the copy's own call. slow_continuation gave the entry block parameters for the copy-defined values live there and renamed uses only in blocks it dominates, so a copy block reachable from the entry through a merge (the join of a conditional, or the shared tail of two sites) still read the copy's original definitions, undefined on the entry path. The baseline compile then failed with 'undefined value vN' and the function stayed interpreted; seen on bench/ash/dyn_dispatch.wren run() once constructor calls in a ternary became sites. Fix: after every site in the loop is done, every copy block takes a parameter for each copy-defined value it reads and every edge passes it (maximal SSA over the copy); the failure edges pass the fast world's values. Reproducer: tests/e2e.rs e2e_inlined_sites_in_a_loop_with_a_merge_compile.","files":null}]}